Kinos
=====

Kinos is a fork of Fladder <https://github.com/DonutWare/Fladder>,
a cross-platform Jellyfin client originally created by DonutWare and
contributors, licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 only
(GPL-3.0-only). The full license text is in the LICENSE file at the
root of this repository, unchanged from upstream.

The GPL covers the code, not the project's name or branding — this fork
is redistributed under a different name (Kinos) precisely because the
license permits it, while every copyright notice from the upstream
project is kept intact below. Nothing in this file removes or narrows
the license under which the original and derived code is distributed.

What changed in this fork, relative to upstream Fladder:
  - Scope narrowed to movies and TV shows only (no music, Live TV,
    e-books, photos, SyncPlay, or remote control features).
  - Platform narrowed to Linux desktop only (Android, iOS, macOS,
    Windows and web builds are not maintained or verified here).
  - Added an integrated Sonarr/Radarr module (library, queue, calendar,
    interactive search) for requesting and managing content directly
    from the client.
  - Renamed throughout (application identifier, package name, visible
    strings) to Kinos.

